1
00:05:30,000 --> 00:05:36,000
He's dying for followers

2
00:11:00,000 --> 00:11:06,000
Deadstream is a horror, comedy film directed by Vanessa Winter.

3
00:16:30,000 --> 00:16:36,000
A disgraced internet personality attempts to win back his followers
by livestreaming one night alone in a haunted house.

4
00:22:00,000 --> 00:22:06,000
But when he accidentally pisses off a vengeful spirit, his big
comeback event becomes a real-time fight for his life.

5
00:27:30,000 --> 00:27:36,000
Shawn, played by Joseph Winter.

6
00:33:00,000 --> 00:33:06,000
Chrissy / Mildred, played by Melanie Stone.

7
00:38:30,000 --> 00:38:36,000
Corner Man / Cop Corpse, played by Jason K. Wixom.

8
00:44:00,000 --> 00:44:06,000
Hettie, played by Pat Barnett Carr.

9
00:49:30,000 --> 00:49:36,000
Max Loland / Cop, played by Marty Collins.

10
00:55:00,000 --> 00:55:06,000
Latin Professor, played by Perla Lacayo.

11
01:00:30,000 --> 01:00:36,000
Deadstream is a 2022 American supernatural horror comedy film directed, written, produced and edited by wife and husband
Vanessa and Joseph Winter in their directorial debut, with Joseph also acting as lead actor and soundtrack composer.

12
01:06:00,000 --> 01:06:06,000
The plot follows a disgraced content creator attempting to resurrect his career by livestreaming himself spending the
night in a notorious haunted house; the film uses a found footage format, displaying the livestream itself.

13
01:11:30,000 --> 01:11:36,000
Deadstream had its world premiere at South by Southwest on March 11, 2022, and was released
in the United States on October 6, 2022, by Shudder to positive reviews.

14
01:17:00,000 --> 01:17:06,000
The film explores themes of haunted house, ghost, found
footage, urbex, social media influencer.

15
01:22:30,000 --> 01:22:36,000
The tone is lighthearted and dark.
